{
  "_toolsNote": "t45: every tool the collector resolves is PINNED here on purpose. Without these keys src/collect.ps1 resolves netstat/netsh/powercfg/tailscale from the real machine (registry, Program Files, PATH) - -NoNative does not gate that - so on a fresh server with no Tailscale the tailscale layer short-circuits to blocked/ts_not_installed and six cases that expect an injected CLI verdict or exitCode 1 fail. The paths are identities, not machine facts: in fixture mode a declared probe is never executed, so only the 'is it installed' branch reads them.",
  "tools": {
    "netstat": "C:\\Windows\\System32\\netstat.exe",
    "netsh": "C:\\Windows\\System32\\netsh.exe",
    "powercfg": "C:\\Windows\\System32\\powercfg.exe",
    "tailscale": "C:\\Program Files\\Tailscale\\tailscale.exe"
  },
  "_comment": "Same machine state as _base/server-en.json, but every tool output is the Chinese (zh-CN) spelling. Used to prove the judgements do not depend on the tool language: netsh section headers, netsh state words, powercfg field names and the sleep-state catalogue are all localized here. Hex indices, GUIDs and the netstat state column are unchanged (the OS itself does not translate those).",
